The `axi_to_reg_v2` module, while greatly improving functionality, incurs rather long paths. 

For example, even when inserting a retimed `axi_cut` right at its input, it still causes the longest (currently violating) path in Cheshire's FPGA implementation, with its `i_axi_to_detailed_mem` claiming more than half the path length alone.

This PR inserts optional (default disabled) mem request and response cuts right after `i_axi_to_detailed_mem`. While this may become quite expensive for large `AxiDataWidth/RegDataWidth`, it should efficiently mitigate timing issues, especially as register interfaces cannot be cut without bandwidth loss.
